1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,040
Japan just launched a spacecraft
日本刚刚发射了一艘飞船，

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,120
to go dig up dirt on a moon of Mars.
要去火星的一颗月亮上挖土。

3
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:05,590
And bring it back to Earth.
然后把土带回地球。

4
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:06,480
A first, ever.
史上第一次。

5
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,970
But this moon has one rule:
可这颗月亮有一条规矩：

6
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:08,760
do not jump.
千万别跳。

7
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,840
Today's question: how do you land on a moon
今天的问题：怎么降落在一颗

8
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,700
where one hop could send you flying?
跳一下就可能飞走的月亮上？

9
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,280
Meet Pho.
认识一下小福。

10
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,450
Phobos, the bigger moon of Mars.
火卫一，福波斯，火星更大的那颗月亮。

11
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:16,360
It's not round.
它不是圆的，

12
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:18,310
It's a lumpy, cratered potato.
像一个坑坑洼洼的土豆。

13
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:19,830
About 22 kilometers across.
宽大约22公里，

14
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:22,430
You could drive across it in twenty minutes.
开车二十分钟就横穿过去了。

15
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:24,690
On October 19th, Japan's H3 rocket
10月19日，日本的H3火箭

16
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:26,670
lifted off from Tanegashima.
从种子岛升空。

17
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:28,420
The mission is called MMX,
任务叫MMX，

18
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:30,300
Martian Moons eXploration.
火星卫星探测。

19
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:31,750
It reaches Mars next August
明年8月到火星，

20
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:33,380
and stays about three years.
在那边待大约三年。

21
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:35,150
It also carries a little robot:
它还带了一个小机器人：

22
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:37,330
a French-German rover called IDEFIX.
法国和德国造的漫游车，IDEFIX。

23
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:39,200
Driving in gravity this weak is tricky:
在这么弱的引力下开车很难：

24
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,960
spin the wheels too hard and the rover could float off.
轮子一使劲，车就可能飘起来。

25
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,630
So it has to move like a sloth,
所以它得像树懒一样，

26
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:44,670
slow and careful.
慢慢地、小心地爬。

27
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:46,130
Twist one: Pho is so light,
反转一：小福太轻了，

28
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:49,280
its gravity is about one seventeen-hundredth of Earth's.
引力只有地球的大约一千七百分之一。

29
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,840
Weigh 60 kilos on Earth?
在地球上60公斤？

30
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:54,350
On Pho you'd weigh about 35 grams. A slice of bread.
在小福上大约只有35克，一片面包那么重。

31
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:57,380
Its escape speed is about 11 meters per second,
逃逸速度大约每秒11米，

32
00:00:57,380 --> 00:00:59,120
roughly 25 miles an hour.
也就是时速40公里左右。

33
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,010
A baseball pitcher
一个棒球投手，

34
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:02,050
could throw a ball right off this moon.
能把球直接扔出这颗月亮。

35
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:04,080
So what about a jump? Our rough math:
那跳一下会怎样？我们粗算一下：

36
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:07,260
a normal jump launches you at about 3 meters per second.
普通人起跳大约每秒3米。

37
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:08,900
You'd float almost a kilometer up
你会飘到快一公里高，

38
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,060
and land more than fifteen minutes later.
十几分钟以后才落回来。

39
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:12,560
Long enough to make a sandwich
够你在半空中

40
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,190
in midair.
做一个三明治。

41
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:14,580
Stand on Pho and look up:
站在小福上抬头看，

42
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,650
Mars fills a huge chunk of the sky.
火星占了一大片天。

43
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:18,170
It looks about 80 times wider
看起来比我们的满月

44
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:19,280
than our full Moon.
宽大约80倍。

45
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:21,940
Pho circles Mars in about seven and a half hours,
小福绕火星一圈只要七个多小时，

46
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:23,310
faster than Mars spins.
比火星自转还快。

47
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:26,250
So from Mars, Pho rises in the west and sets in the east,
所以在火星上看，小福西边升起、东边落下，

48
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:26,990
twice a day.
一天两次。

49
00:01:26,990 --> 00:01:28,420
Twist two: Pho is so light,
反转二：小福这么轻，

50
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:31,090
a spacecraft can't even orbit it the normal way.
飞船连正常地绕着它转都做不到。

51
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:32,440
Pho is so close to Mars
小福离火星太近了，

52
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:35,210
that Mars' gravity drags the spacecraft away.
火星的引力会把飞船拽走。

53
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:36,640
So MMX uses a trick:
所以MMX耍了个花招：

54
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,480
a quasi-satellite orbit.
准卫星轨道。

55
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,450
The spacecraft actually orbits Mars,
飞船其实是在绕火星转，

56
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,050
sticking right next to Pho.
只是一直跟在小福身边。

57
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:44,340
Seen from Pho, it seems to circle around it.
从小福看过去，飞船好像在绕着自己转圈。

58
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:47,060
Like two runners on a track, weaving side by side.
就像跑道上两个并排跑、来回交错的人。

59
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:48,430
Then it touches down twice
然后它会降落两次，

60
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:51,300
and uses a puff of gas to blow dirt into a canister.
用一股气把土吹进罐子里。

61
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:53,570
In gravity this weak, every push pushes back.
在这么弱的引力下，你推地面，地面也推你。

62
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:55,760
Dig too hard, and you shove yourself off.
挖得太猛，就把自己推飞了。

63
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,690
The goal: about 10 grams of dirt.
目标：大约10克土。

64
00:01:57,690 --> 00:01:59,040
Roughly a tablespoon.
差不多一勺。

65
00:01:59,040 --> 00:01:59,600
In 2031,
2031年，

66
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:02,170
that tablespoon lands in Australia.
这一勺土会落在澳大利亚。

67
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:04,450
Before heading home, it will also fly past
临走前，它还会顺路看一眼

68
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:06,410
Mars' other, smaller moon, Deimos.
火星另一颗更小的月亮，火卫二。

69
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:07,540
Why all this trouble?
为什么这么费劲？

70
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:09,870
Because nobody knows where Pho came from.
因为没人知道小福是从哪来的。

71
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:11,340
One idea: it's an asteroid
一种说法：它是一颗小行星，

72
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,540
that Mars captured.
被火星抓住了。

73
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:14,240
Another idea: a giant impact
另一种说法：一次大撞击，

74
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:16,310
knocked a chunk off Mars itself.
从火星身上撞下来一块。

75
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:18,050
That tablespoon could settle it.
那一勺土可能会给出答案。

76
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:19,920
It might even hold bits of Mars.
里面也许还有火星本身的碎渣。

77
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,360
Twist three, the sad part:
反转三，最惨：

78
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,310
Pho is falling.
小福正在往下掉。

79
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:25,330
It orbits only about 6,000 kilometers above Mars,
它离火星表面只有大约六千公里，

80
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:28,480
and creeps about 2 centimeters closer every year.
每年靠近大约两厘米。

81
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:31,010
Blame tides: Mars' gravity drags Pho inward,
怪潮汐：火星的引力把小福一点点往里拖，

82
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:32,920
like a slowly tightening lasso.
像一个慢慢收紧的绳套。

83
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,390
In tens of millions of years,
几千万年以后，

84
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:36,650
Mars will tear it apart, or it will crash.
它会被火星撕碎，或者直接撞上去。

85
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:39,100
Mars might even end up with a ring of its own.
到时候，火星也许会有一圈自己的光环。

86
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:40,720
That's one scientific guess.
这是科学家的一种推测。

87
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:43,050
Friendly fine print: MMX won't jump.
友情提示：MMX不会跳。

88
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:45,320
It sets down gently, on its legs.
它会用腿，轻轻地落下去。

89
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,470
So we'd better hurry
所以我们得趁早，

90
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:48,720
and grab a souvenir before Pho falls.
赶在小福掉下去之前，拿一勺土当纪念。

91
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,540
And Pho's one rule still stands:
小福的规矩还是那一条：

92
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:51,570
do not jump.
千万别跳。

